#Other Information
#1.  All depths are referenced to driller's pipe tally unless
#    otherwise noted.
#
#2.  All data presented are recorded in memory data unless
#    otherwise stated.
#
#3.  No depth corrections have been made for pipe stretch or
#    compression.
#
#4.  Environmental parameters used in Gamma Ray & Resistivity
#    processing:
#    Hole Size                   - 8.50" (Fixed Hole Size)
#    Tool Size                   - 6.75"
#    Mud Weight                  - 10.20 ppg
#    KCL Concentration           - 8 pbw
#    Mud Resistivity             - 2000 ohm
#
#    Environmental parameters used in ALD & CTN processing:
#    Hole size                   - 8.50" (Fixed Hole Size)
#    Tool Size                   - 6.75"
#    Mud Weight                  - 10.20 ppg
#    Pressure                    - Hydrostatic Pressure
#    Formation Water Salinity    - 7888 ppm Cl-
#    Formation Matrix            - SS / 2.65 g/cc
#    Mud Type                    - Synthetic Oil Based Mud
#    Whole Mud Chlorides         - 14319 - 48123 ppm
#    Temperature                 - 41.50°C - 103.92°C
#
#5.  Curve mnemonics used in this log - (Filtering)
#    Even interval Every=0.1524m - Smoothed @ 0.2m -Gap fill=3m
#
#    ROPA   :Avg Rate of Penetration
#    DGRCC  :DGR Comb Gamma Ray BCorr
#    R09PC  :09in Phase Resistivity BC (Extra-Shallow Spacing)
#    R15PC  :15in Phase Resistivity BC (Shallow Spacing)
#    R27PC  :27in Phase Resistivity BC (Medium Spacing)
#    R39PC  :39in Phase Resistivity BC (Deep Spacing)
#    R39AC  :39in Atten Resistivity BC (Deep Spacing)
#    EWXT   :EWR Formation Exp Time 
#    EWTEMP :EWR Temperature
#    TNPL   :CTN Porosity Limestone
#    ALCDA  :ALD Average Comp Density
#    ALDCA  :ALD Average Den Corr
#    ALPEA  :ALD Average Pe Factor
#    ALHSI  :ALD Hole Size Indicator
#
#
#6.  EWR-P4 Near to Far Receiver -6"
#    R09PC to Near Receiver      -6"   (2Mhz)
#    R15PC to Near Receiver      -12"  (2Mhz)
#    R27PC to Near Receiver      -24"  (1Mhz)
#    R39PC to Near Receiver      -36"  (1Mhz)
#
#7. Run 1100 was a 8.50" PDC bit rotary steerable BHA with 
#   6.75" DIR-GR-RES-PWD-DENS-PORS from Well B25ST3. Wiped 
#   depth interval from 518.00m MD to 531.00m MD and drilled 
#   the 8.50" hole section from 531.00m MD (493.23m TVD) to 
#   1678.00m MD (1068.90m TVD) with 10.20 ppg enhanced lime 
#   polymer water-based mud. The BHA was lost in hole during 
#   POOH operation. Data presented is realtime data only.
#
#8. Run 1200 was a 8.50" PDC bit rotary steerable BHA with 
#   6.75" DIR-GR-RES-PWD-DENS-PORS. Drilled the 8.50" hole 
#   section from 640.00m MD (575.99m TVD) to 2159.00m MD  
#   (1245.74m TVD) with 10.20 ppg oil-based mud. POOH for 
#   7" casing.
#
#9. Well B25ST4 reached TD at 2159.00m MD / 1245.74m TVD.
#
#
